## Claim
Text: "India's imports from China increased by 27% during the period April-August 2020."
Claim author: Pankaj Pachauri
Claim date: October 19, 2020
Claim origin: https://twitter.com/PankajPachauri/status/1318185530786459648

## Initial Q&A
### Did India's imports from China increase by 27% during the period from April to August 2020, according to official trade data?
Answer: No, according to official trade data cited by Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal in Parliament, India's imports from China actually **declined** by 27.63% during April-August 2020-21 compared to the same period the previous year, falling to $21.58 billion. As the source states, "India's imports from China have declined by 27.63 per cent during April-August, 2020-21 over the corresponding period of the previous year." The claim incorrectly states the change was an increase of 27%, when in fact it was a decrease of approximately 27.63%.

Source URL: https://www.businesstoday.in/current/economy-politics/imports-from-china-decline-by-27-63-during-april-august-2020-piyush-goyal/story/416674.html

